 "caveats": [
  "SURVIVOR BIAS: survivors-only backtest universe, so CAGR is an UPPER BOUND. Of ~721 S&P names that left the index 2011-2026, only ~40 are genuine bankruptcies (the rest are M&A / ticker-changes, NOT losses) and are excluded from the panel. The failure-bias is bounded (momentum/quality screens avoid most pre-bankruptcy names) but real - not a survivorship-free track record.",
  "Backtested 2011-2026 on the BROAD universe (no floor; trading = eligible), NOT a forward projection. Realistic forward ~25-29%; per-2yr regime CAGR 8% to 48% (median 21%).",
  "E3/PEAD is the validated core: real post-earnings drift (survives zeroing announcement-window days), entered 3 days AFTER the filing \u2014 reacts to earnings, does not predict them.",
  "Liquidity-survival 0.96 at a $5M-ADV lens \u2014 the edge is tradeable, not a microcap artifact (unlike the .7-event tilt it replaced).",
  "TRUE daily mark-to-market: the -48% drawdown is the real intra-period low. Top-3 concentration = high single-name risk (179 distinct names rotated over the backtest).",
  "Frictionless backtest: ignores ~778%/yr turnover cost, slippage, tax. LIVE forward paper-track (separate, vs SPY) begins 2026-07-01."
 ]
}